  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#35486\", \"PowerToys#35375\", \"PowerToys#48785\"], \"answer\": \"Your ticket doesn't give any details. It looks like earlier reports that the Text Extractor shortcut (default Win+Shift+T) does nothing. The archive has no confirmed fix, but those tickets point to these things to try:\\n1. Open Text Extractor from the PowerToys tray icon or the Settings window. In one ticket this worked, and the shortcut then started working again for a while. Another ticket reports that PowerToys needs to be running, or its Settings window open, for hotkeys to respond.\\n2. Check for shortcut conflicts. Win+Shift+T clashes with a Windows taskbar shortcut, and Win+Shift+Q is taken by Keyboard Manager by default. Try a different activation shortcut in the Text Extractor settings.\\n3. Restart PowerToys and make sure the Text Extractor module is enabled.\\n4. If it still fails, add steps to reproduce and a PowerToys bug report ZIP (from the Settings window) to your ticket. The maintainers asked for this in similar cases.\"}",
